#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "455280a6-f859-5054-803b-696ef3129529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=42,y=-35,z=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331137} {:answer/id #uuid "d84f689a-134f-5407-b5f7-e046f6e72b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331138} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0c1bfc-c0b0-5476-9eff-a10057ad340a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331139} {:answer/id #uuid "49684f5f-864b-59c5-b876-5b3a8697f322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=19,y=49,z=58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331140} {:answer/id #uuid "ac85153a-3e2f-5e94-8d8d-4602905ebb9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac85153a-3e2f-5e94-8d8d-4602905ebb9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331141} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1033273-5d4f-5a9d-b005-946c4dd7384e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f56f052-82ef-5f6f-b9cb-411952681c67" :question/math-academy-id "q-10076" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z=9 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ -49 \\\\ -58\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=19,y=-49,z=-58.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "567483a4-8d5d-5829-8cd3-4512c59f9513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=-4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340842} {:answer/id #uuid "a66b9fd9-30c2-52c7-98f3-cb09d55a8e9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,y=8,z=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340843} {:answer/id #uuid "a496caee-0e84-52e6-9a1e-84aaa4a7e232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340844} {:answer/id #uuid "c678093b-aa73-555b-b056-7c362def00ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5,y=8,z=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340845} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ef49ce-ebaa-5ef1-9a27-37da3f989153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a496caee-0e84-52e6-9a1e-84aaa4a7e232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340844} :answer-field/id #uuid "b17aa334-95a3-5fed-9246-3dcdbe01c49d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cdfb00b-0ec5-5b97-84f5-0f56716105ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-10102" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+2z=1 \\\\ x+y+z=3 \\\\ y+2z=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2(2)+2(1) \\\\  & =-4+2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 4 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Matrix Equation Using Algebraic Manipulation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a76f811-4fb7-588a-8e60-a9a90d8b3d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340849} {:answer/id #uuid "fbdaed99-aabc-5d6f-bd7e-29f69039b884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340850} {:answer/id #uuid "32d5f4f7-c9c0-56a9-b9ea-51a0a16fd6c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340851} {:answer/id #uuid "08b9f127-1081-5f1b-bf9a-b291ff746685" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32d5f4f7-c9c0-56a9-b9ea-51a0a16fd6c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340851} :answer-field/id #uuid "b01113f5-b230-5cc2-bb1e-fca70e3b531d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d11cc235-a86a-5cde-9c79-1a294e9c7835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340854} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0b3172-c200-58ec-851f-dbb391743e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340855} {:answer/id #uuid "d0716dd7-2e7b-522e-bc5e-51afc9e859ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340856} {:answer/id #uuid "21af412b-c03f-578d-a853-12f2260c8bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f0b3172-c200-58ec-851f-dbb391743e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340855} :answer-field/id #uuid "001f9419-dbba-5bf1-8010-931a2d54adb7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca13a177-8a64-5ce2-aabf-e219ebbc1f18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340859} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3adf99-bc81-5acf-bc04-908f6c62ec17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340860} {:answer/id #uuid "3a81284f-b9f3-5257-aa66-6bb82828bdda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "bA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340861} {:answer/id #uuid "8cbccb15-b7aa-56db-ae70-06471bee8ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Ab" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca3adf99-bc81-5acf-bc04-908f6c62ec17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340860} :answer-field/id #uuid "68320e58-def6-5e19-88bd-d116147ae876" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340858} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "439a98aa-443e-55d0-9926-2bad3ac72958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{I}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340864} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b1ebed-4ab8-50e4-9bf9-c1b2ca670090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340865} {:answer/id #uuid "aabd9b00-3787-5ff6-9f73-a0b73c7b6aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340866} {:answer/id #uuid "c62473cc-e969-5660-9451-1fb2cfad8a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c62473cc-e969-5660-9451-1fb2cfad8a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340867} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4bf8e22-a4fb-524a-b34f-476d3062e5ab" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0061045b-9889-5cff-9c20-3d54327e1d3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-317900" :question/problem "Consider a system of $3$ linear equations in $3$ variables, written in matrix form as $A\\,x=b.$ Here, $A$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $x$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $b$ is the column vector containing the constants. What are the missing parts of the derivation method shown below to find the unique solution of the system?\n\n$$\nA\\,x={{field-1}}\n$$\n\n$$\n{{field-2}}\\,x={A}^{-1}\\,b\n$$\n\n$$\n{I}_{3}\\,x={A}^{-1}\\,{{field-3}}\n$$\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}={A}^{-1}\\,b\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A\\,x=b$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\,x & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}A\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,b \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}\\,b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Matrix Equation Using Algebraic Manipulation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "399b2205-9b7b-5bfd-945a-ef5eefeecb13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=BA\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340870} {:answer/id #uuid "e6686259-76b5-5ceb-a5ef-72cce0cbf73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340871} {:answer/id #uuid "876074ae-763b-53ee-91b5-462af323933c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340872} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b6a13b-2635-5dfd-9231-110608a8e0ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340873} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2e17be-9561-51ae-becd-6a6de9a2d231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}\\,d\\,B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0b6a13b-2635-5dfd-9231-110608a8e0ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340873} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c8bfe68-6156-5af6-a3c1-c07ca6cc0947" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ecb9056c-9932-5a89-8f17-1df1e929dfe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-78445" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $AB\\,x=d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $4\\times 4$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $4\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $AB\\,x=d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB\\,x & =d \\\\ {A}^{-1}AB\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{4}B\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ B\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${B}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,x={A}^{-1}\\,d$ by ${B}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{4}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271ccdef-55c9-5cd2-9341-32528cbed4ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340877} {:answer/id #uuid "ec731dd3-6cf7-5c80-b355-010517a42eff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340878} {:answer/id #uuid "dade19ea-899c-5f22-ab0b-f56bd2c25566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340879} {:answer/id #uuid "3bce034f-0376-586a-9ec5-6bef947db9b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340880} {:answer/id #uuid "5aaca2b1-a589-525d-9849-b5b3584b7ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dade19ea-899c-5f22-ab0b-f56bd2c25566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340879} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1a59596-119a-5937-9d9d-686d733c76e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a73bb8b3-8d6b-591a-b918-191402786b60" :question/math-academy-id "q-78555" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x-y-z=3 \\\\ 6x-3y-5z=5 \\\\ 5x-y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & 9 & -16 \\\\ 9 & -7 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & 9 & -16 \\\\ 9 & -7 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=-5,z=2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+(-5)+2=-3.$"}]}
